# P4.17 — проверка coherent Prepare/authority

Pre-implementation base: cb3b897b30cbe0bc3f5816a20878be9064974f99.

Static lookup precedes source resolution. Static PolicyOnly uses the original catalog/frame and invokes no assignment/dynamic/state capability, even in an unrecognized authority transaction (existing FenceTest control).

A static miss on an opt-in panel enters a complete read attempt. Explicit non-global tenant/context is refused before authority storage until the structural boundary implementation. Source-level tenant tests call permissions(panel, exact TenantRef) directly; they do not claim scoped Authorizer integration.

Attempt sequence:

1. Start from the original static catalog and operation frame, preserving original request/now/build/actor. Create fresh sessions/state-map/definition/contribution arrays.
2. Pin each DB read handle to PanelSettings::reads; collect every consumed source's T_before before any dynamic lookup.
3. Fully materialize exact panel/tenant definitions, construct a new overlay; validate Grants-only authority, names and static/prefix conflicts.
4. If the action exists, materialize all relevant grants/role capabilities on the pinned sessions. Other sources are read before the DB fence closes.
5. Read all T_after on those handles. A changed token discards overlay, contributions, errors and state-map together and restarts from step 1. Three unstable attempts give ConsistencyError with no accepted DB state.
6. A stable unknown action throws UnknownPermissionException; a wildcard grant cannot create a definition. A stable source/definition error gives SourceError. Authority qualifies accepted contributions without a second DB read/fence; only accepted DB state and source revisions enter the new frame.

Synthetic interference after role_grants changes the label and removes grants. The asserted read sequence is exactly:

`state → definitions → direct → roles → state → state → definitions → direct → roles → state`

The retried metadata is New and the retried contribution set is empty. Calling Authority on the prepared frame adds no authority reads. A separate source callback modifying DB verifies that T_after covers other sources as well. A disappeared action never uses its old grant. The retry-cap test asserts exactly three attempts. The Default fixture uses a different SQLite PDO with version 17/Replica metadata/no grants while Primary has Old metadata/an exact grant.

Coverage: DynamicCatalogTest, DynamicFenceTest and existing FenceTest. Source-level A/B/global/foreign-panel definitions and assignments use exact tenant pairs; static roles and snapshots are shared. Replacing an overlay drops old definitions/owners and keeps the static namespace index.

Boundaries retained from accepted D15/D16: scoped end-to-end/P08 is P4.18; structural tenant/context boundary is P4.6; cache/refresh is P4.8; dynamic writes/events/cleanup are P5.3; recognized transaction protocol is P4.20; real races/replica windows are P4.21. No new write manager, cache, scope grant or strict replica freshness is claimed.
